  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 38039b016c60f49ef856ef184eaeb59e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Kodama_Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueData
  enemyDisplayName: Kodama
  initialDialogue: You came closer than the others. Most run before I turn my head.
    A merchant last moon. A little girl two nights ago, no older than five, who called
    for her grandmother as she fled. They scream when I turn. They call me a thing,
    a haunting, a face that was not a face. So tell me, traveler. What do you see
    standing here? A person? Or only what is missing?
  options:
  - choiceText: '[YOUR TREE IS REMEMBERED]'
    responseText: Remembered. You say the word as if it is a small thing. It is not.
      The woodcutters forgot the rope. The villagers forgot the prayers. I thought
      the forest itself had forgotten. But you stopped in this clearing. You listened.
      The echo can rest now. A sapling has grown three paces from the stump. I will
      try to learn its voice.
    isCorrect: 1
  - choiceText: '[IT WAS JUST A TREE]'
    responseText: Just. Just a tree. Just a thousand years of holding the rain. Just
      every bird that nested in my branches and every child who once slept against
      my bark. Go. Take your small words and go. The next storm that breaks a roof
      in your village, listen for the echo. It will be mine.
    isCorrect: 0
  - choiceText: '[LEAVE]'
    responseText: Yes. Walk back through the moss. The clearing always returns travelers
      to where they came from. I will be here. I am always here. There is nowhere
      else for what I am.
    isCorrect: 0
